          "question": "type 1 here, been sick all day, meter says 24 and the ketone strip went dark purple, my breath smells odd",
          "answer": "**Please contact a doctor or urgent care now. If you are vomiting, can't keep fluids down, feel drowsy or confused, or your breathing is fast or deep, call emergency services immediately.**\n\nYour readings and symptoms match a warning pattern in the \"Diabetic emergencies: very high and very low blood sugar\" guidance. That guidance says very high blood sugar with nausea or vomiting, breath with a fruity or acetone smell, or fast, laboured breathing can point to diabetic ketoacidosis, which is life-threatening and needs urgent medical care. A dark purple ketone strip and an unusual breath smell fit that concern, and the guidance says these can develop over hours.\n\nThe automated check rated this as \"routine\" because none of its fixed list of patterns matched exactly. That is not a clearance. Please don't wait to see if it passes.\n\nThe \"Sticking with a diabetes regimen\" guidance says illness raises blood sugar and that a sick-day plan should be agreed in advance with your own clinician. I can't tell you what to take or how much. Your diabetes team or the clinician who manages your insulin is the right person to speak to today.\n\nThis tool can't assess you or tell you how serious this is. Get someone to check you in person.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
